                <pb facs="0615" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.192/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Panama</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">South</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-01-30T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>11. Your 11, January 29, 3 p.m. You may inform Panaman Government that this
                    Government is willing to appoint a Commission to negotiate treaty with Panaman
                    Commission and is willing to commence negotiations in Washington at convenience
                    of Panaman Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
